ect Rigs of Rods and was initially released as a tech demo in 2013 before moving to Steam Early Access in 2015. Players can engage in campaigns, time trials, and free roam across various open-world maps, experimenting with vehicle collisions, environmental physics, and user-created mods. The game supports VR, features an integration with the car-building game Automation, and has native modding support with a community repository.", "themes": [{"id": 1, "name": "Action"}, {"id": 33, "name": "Sandbox"}], "url": "https://www.igdb.com/games/beamng-dot-drive", "videos": [{"id": 130970, "name": "Trailer", "video_id": "4ms-LHkN6YQ", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4ms-LHkN6YQ", "title": "BeamNG.drive - Showreel Trailer", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/4ms-LHkN6YQ/maxresdefault.jpg"}, {"id": 185111, "name": "Announcement Trailer", "video_id": "83mWWlAXJQY", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=83mWWlAXJQY", "title": "BeamNG.drive - Announcement Trailer | PS5 Games", "thumb": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/83mWWlAXJQY/maxresdefault.jpg"}]}